<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  API 31+ only. Complements android:allowBackup="false" in the manifest; it
  does not replace it. allowBackup="false" disables cloud Auto Backup and
  `adb backup`, but on some OEMs it does NOT stop device-to-device transfer
  (e.g. Samsung Smart Switch, Google Quick Start); see
  https://developer.android.com/identity/data/autobackup. The
  device-transfer exclusion below is what actually blocks that path on
  API 31+. Do not remove either mechanism thinking the other makes it
  redundant.

  Domain coverage: per the doc above, domain="root" only covers the
  getFilesDir()/getDatabasePath()/SharedPreferences subtree; it does NOT
  cover domain="external" (getExternalFilesDir()) or the device-protected
  storage domains (device_root, device_file, device_database,
  device_sharedpref); those are sibling domains, not children of root.
  Each is excluded explicitly below in both sections so none of the app's
  storage areas are missed.

  Known gap this file cannot close: exported recordings written to shared
  storage (per the README, Music/Recordings via MediaStore) live outside
  every domain listed above; MediaStore/shared storage is not part of
  the dataExtractionRules domain model at all. If those exports need to be
  excluded from cloud backup or device transfer, that is a separate
  decision to be made in the export path itself (e.g. how/where it writes),
  not something this file can express.

  Residual gap on API 29-30 (this app's minSdk; see the minSdk value in
  app/build.gradle.kts, which is the source of truth; if it is raised to
  31+ this whole comment block should be revisited): dataExtractionRules is
  API 31+ only and has no effect below that. The legacy
  android:fullBackupContent mechanism governs backup *content* on 29-30 (it
  is not documented, in the page cited above or elsewhere we've checked, to
  control OEM device-to-device transfer specifically; treat that as
  unconfirmed rather than settled). On 29-30 this app relies on
  allowBackup="false" alone for the device-to-device transfer path, which
  is a known, deliberate, accepted tradeoff: raising minSdk to 31 to close
  this gap would cost real device reach, and the residual exposure requires
  physical access to an unlocked device plus a deliberate user-initiated
  transfer.
-->
<data-extraction-rules>
    <cloud-backup>
        <exclude domain="root" path="." />
        <exclude domain="external" path="." />
        <exclude domain="device_root" path="." />
        <exclude domain="device_file" path="." />
        <exclude domain="device_database" path="." />
        <exclude domain="device_sharedpref" path="." />
    </cloud-backup>
    <device-transfer>
        <exclude domain="root" path="." />
        <exclude domain="external" path="." />
        <exclude domain="device_root" path="." />
        <exclude domain="device_file" path="." />
        <exclude domain="device_database" path="." />
        <exclude domain="device_sharedpref" path="." />
    </device-transfer>
</data-extraction-rules>
